  "title": "Mary Reibey",
  "summary": "Born in Bury, Lancashire, in 1777, Mary Reibey was sentenced to transportation after being arrested over a stolen horse and arrived in Sydney as a convict on the Royal Admiral in 1792. She married Thomas Reibey in 1794, and after his death in 1811 ran warehouses and ships as a wealthy Sydney businesswoman and philanthropist. She died in Newtown, Sydney, in 1855.",
